{"path":"locale/collate/transform","title":"std::collate<CharT>::transform, do_transform","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::collate&lt;CharT&gt;::</span>transform, do_transform","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale/collate/transform","section":"locale","kind":"page","summary":"The string transformed so that lexicographic comparison of the transformed strings may be used instead of collating of the originals.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/locale\">&lt;locale&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">public</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br>string_type transform<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> CharT<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> low, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> CharT<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> high <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">protected</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> string_type do_transform<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> CharT<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> low, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> CharT<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> high <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Public member function, calls the protected virtual member function <code>do_transform</code> of the most derived class.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Converts the character sequence <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">low</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">high</span></code><code>)</code></span> to a string that, compared lexicographically (e.g. with <code>operator&lt;</code> for strings) with the result of calling <code>transform()</code> on another string, produces the same result as calling <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/collate/compare\">do_compare()</a></span> on the same two strings.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> low\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the first character in the sequence to transform\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> high\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> one past the end pointer for the sequence to transform\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The string transformed so that lexicographic comparison of the transformed strings may be used instead of collating of the originals. In the \"C\" locale, the returned string is the exact copy of <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">low</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">high</span></code><code>)</code></span>. In other locales, the contents of the returned string are implementation-defined, and the size may be considerably longer.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>In addition to the use in collation, the implementation-specific format of the transformed string is known to <a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/regex_traits/transform_primary\">std::regex_traits&lt;&gt;::transform_primary</a>, which is able to extract the equivalence class information.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iomanip&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;locale&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/locale/global\"><span class=\"kw2701\">std::<span class=\"me2\">locale</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">global</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/locale\"><span class=\"kw1911\">std::<span class=\"me2\">locale</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"sv_SE.utf8\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> f <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/use_facet\"><span class=\"kw1914\">std::<span class=\"me2\">use_facet</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/collate\"><span class=\"kw1960\">std::<span class=\"me2\">collate</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">wchar_t</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/locale\"><span class=\"kw1911\">std::<span class=\"me2\">locale</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1240\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wstring</span></span></a> in1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> L<span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es3\">\\u00e4</span>ngel\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1240\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wstring</span></span></a> in2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> L<span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es3\">\\u00e5</span>r\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1240\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wstring</span></span></a> out1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> f.<span class=\"me1\">transform</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>in1<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>, <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>in1<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> in1.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1240\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wstring</span></span></a> out2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> f.<span class=\"me1\">transform</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>in2<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>, <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>in2<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> in2.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"In the Swedish locale: \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>out1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> out2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" before \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" before \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"In lexicographic comparison: \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>in1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> in2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" before \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1776\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" before \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>In the Swedish locale: år before ängel\nIn lexicographic comparison: ängel before år</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strxfrm\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strxfrm</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  transform a string so that <code>strcmp</code> would produce the same result as <code>strcoll</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/wide/wcsxfrm\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wcsxfrm</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  transform a wide string so that <code>wcscmp</code> would produce the same result as <code>wcscoll</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"locale","title":"Localization library"},{"path":"locale/collate","title":"std::collate"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::collate<CharT>::transform, do_transform","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Public member function, calls the protected virtual member function do_transform of the most derived class."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"low, high"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The string transformed so that lexicographic comparison of the transformed strings may be used instead of collating of the originals."},{"label":"Notes","note":"In addition to the use in collation, the implementation-specific format of the transformed string is known to std::regex_traits<>::transform_primary, which is…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"strxfrm","note":"transform a string so that strcmp would produce the same result as strcoll"},{"label":"wcsxfrm","note":"transform a wide string so that wcscmp would produce the same result as wcscoll"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":341,"codeBlockCount":2}
